LICENCE
=======

Copyright (c) University of Bristol.

This repository is REUSE-compliant (https://reuse.software/): the licence and
copyright holder of every file are recorded in `REUSE.toml`, and the licence
texts are in `LICENSES/`. It follows the licensing of the documentation
repository, https://github.com/isambard-sc/docs.isambard.ac.uk, which is the
authoritative source (see "Licences used" in its CONTRIBUTING.md).

| Licence      | Applies to                                                         |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| CC-BY-SA-4.0 | Skills (all files under `site/plugins/isambard/skills/`) and `README.md` |
| MIT          | Code and tooling: `.github/workflows/` and `site/index.html`       |
| CC0-1.0      | Agent helpers (`.github/agents/`), editor, plugin and site configuration, and this file |

Skills are derived from https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/, whose pages (including
the policy pages) are CC-BY-SA-4.0. Each skill also states its licence in the
`license` field of its `SKILL.md` frontmatter.

Attribution for skills: "Markdown/image content derived from
https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/, (c) 2024 University of Bristol."

Licence texts:

  * CC-BY-SA-4.0: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
  * MIT:          LICENSES/MIT.txt
  * CC0-1.0:      LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt

The BriCS logos, favicons and HPE PDFs in the documentation repository are all
rights reserved there. None of that material is included in this repository.

When adding a file, use the licence that matches its type and add it to
`REUSE.toml` (or give it an SPDX header). Run `reuse lint` to check.
